    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Javan,<div>this may not have anything to do with your problem (I&#39;ve only quickly glanced at your code) but I know that dnebgin() can be somewhat temperamental. You may want to try describing the Negative Binomial as a Poisson-Gamma mixture instead. There is an example for how to do that on the JAGS forum (<a href=\"https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/610037/thread/31ae7acb/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/610037/thread/31ae7acb/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792494542626000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3s8lE1rKNTQVwISRpnB_5w\">https://sourceforge.net/p/mcmc-jags/discussion/610037/thread/31ae7acb/</a> ).</div><div>Best</div><div>Rahel</div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Jun 5, 2019 at 4:55 AM Javan Bauder &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">javanv...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
